# CR 601.2h/106.6: {1}{W} from a pool holding two white and one red -- the
# white pip spends a white mana, and the one unit of generic is answered
# from the red rather than any fixed leftover order (manapay.go,
# ChoosePayGeneric).
# Main phase of turn 1, so the payment is made at a priority (L2 S19); the
# lands are tapped there, since a pool loaded by setup.state empties as the
# steps pass (CR 500.4).
startturn human
advance 3
tapformana human 1 W
tapformana human 2 W
tapformana human 3 R
queue paygeneric R
paymanacost human 1 W
